0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 198 Tm /F1 10 Tf 13 TL (Reverse Universe Theory \(RUT\) is a proposed geometric cosmology framework in which cosmic expansion,) Tj T* (structure growth, lensing response, light propagation, and time-directionality are treated as measurable) Tj T* (expressions of a shared transition structure. This paper does not attempt to test the full RUT framework.) Tj T* (Instead, it isolates a reduced observational bridge model and compares it with LambdaCDM in background,) Tj T* (growth, and growth-lensing diagnostics. The reduced bridge is encoded by B\(a\) = 1/2[1 + tanh\(\(a - a_t\)/Delta) Tj T* (a\)], with a growth response mu\(a\) = 1 + mu0 B\(a\) and a lensing response Sigma\(a\) = 1 + lambda_Sigma mu0) Tj T* (B\(a\). Earlier background and growth tests showed that RUT is stable and mock-detectable, but that current) Tj T* (background and joint growth data do not provide a decisive advantage over LambdaCDM. The strongest) Tj T* (current result appears in the E_G growth-lensing lane. In a pilot diagonal E_G compilation, fixed neutral-lensing) Tj T* (RUT, defined by lambda_Sigma = 0, improves the fit relative to LambdaCDM. The result survives) Tj T* (one-measurement-per-family reduction, family-weighted averaging, and leave-one-point-out jackknife tests. In) Tj T* (the hardened pilot packet, fixed neutral RUT gives Delta BIC approximately -2.108 in the full diagonal) Tj T* (compilation, approximately -1.926 in the one-per-family subset, approximately -1.963 in the family-weighted) Tj T* (subset, and wins 18/18 leave-one-point-out jackknife runs. We do not claim a detection. The analysis remains) Tj T* (diagonal-only and not covariance-clean. The result is presented as a reproducible pilot signal and a target for) Tj T* (independent, covariance-controlled testing.) Tj T* ET
Q
